              "question": "<p>There are four types of hypersensitivity reactions. Which of the following is termed \"a true allergy\", and can be successfully treated with antihistamines and/or adrenaline injection? (it is treated with adrenaline and antihistamines if it causes widespread anaphylaxis, or treated with antihistamines if a local reaction such as allergic rhinitis (hay fever).</p>\n"
            },
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "metadata": {
              "contentType": "Multiple Choice",
              "license": "U",
              "title": "Untitled Multiple Choice"
            },
            "subContentId": "c2e8e5b1-1946-4ad4-8480-a46059973139"
          },
          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NO, Histamine constricts the airways. This reaction was probably developed as the body's way of stopping further allergens to get into the body.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Indeed,&nbsp;Histamine constricts the airways. This reaction was probably developed as the body's way of stopping further allergens to get into the body.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Histamine dilates the bronchi</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Histamine Dilates the blood vessels</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Histamine makes the blood vessels more permeable, leading to oedema (locally or systemically, depending on how extensive the reaction is)</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Histamine is released from mast cells (a local reaction) and basophils (a systemic reaction) in response to the allergen</div>\n"
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
