              "question": "<p>A colleague just had a needle stick injury with an EpiPen (adrenaline injector) into her finger. She should consider a follow up of phentolamine (an adrenaline antagonist) into that local area to prevent necrosis, because adrenaline is such a strong constrictor of blood vessels that she could loose the tip of her finger.&nbsp;</p>\n"
